API Gateway: A Comprehensive 35-Minute High-Level Design Presentation

Research-oriented technical presentation · Senior / Lead Backend Engineer ·
Java 21 · Spring Boot · Distributed Systems · Production Architecture

This expanded version goes beyond a conventional system-design interview answer. 
It develops the API Gateway as an architectural problem: 
  - its role in a distributed system, 
  - internal request-processing model, 
  - implementation alternatives, 
  - mathematical capacity analysis, 
  - resilience engineering, 
  - security boundaries,
  - consistency trade-offs, 
  - operational failure modes, 
  - and research questions.

The presentation is organized so that you can deliver it aloud in 35 minutes,
explain why each architectural decision is justified, and defend those decisions under detailed questioning.
