1.3 Non-functional requirements
    These are the qualities that make this a senior-level design problem.
        - Availability: A gateway failure must not take the entire platform offline unnecessarily.
        - Low latency: Gateway processing should consume only a controlled part of the end-to-end latency budget.
        - Horizontal scalability: Capacity should grow by adding gateway instances.
        - Security: Backend services should not be directly exposed unintentionally.
        - Resilience: A slow Payment Service should not consume all gateway resources.
        - Operability: Engineers should be able to identify which route or downstream dependency is failing.
        - Maintainability: Routing and security policy changes should not require rewriting the entire gateway.

